commentBody:
@SPI

I got it very quickly in the upper left, not insignificantly aided by the revealer or two wedged right up there.  It just took me a minute to get that it was a dead simple game of reverse rather than reordering anything.

Maybe this is the optimal angelic form of constructor's crossword. The ones I've seen until now have been despicable in that they were tortuous to the customer while in search of meaningless inside baseball brownie points like pangrams ad lengthiness stunts....  This one was lighthearted and didn't strike me as exclusive at all.  It was fun, if way too easy.

