@HeathieJ
Great timing, Heathie, with Rosh Ha-shanah/ Jewish New Year barrelling down at us Jews in a shockingly few weeks.
Maimonides (1100s, Spain; big name in this field of thought) said that repentance /תשובה, /lit./ 'returning' requires:
- remorse, i.e., the internal realisation of the pointlessness and waste involved in the sin and the resolution never to do it again;
- confession, i.e., the verbal statement of remorse to the injured party or in public (as in prayers); 
- atonement, i.e., the act of making whole the injured party and making peace with them.
For traditionally observant Jews, the month before R"H should be called "Awkward Conversations-ember." 🙄

