@Moira
If you ever lived in Texas--or, well, just visited San Antonio--you wouldn't even ask/exclaim about this clue/entry.  Many prominent figures in Texas  history died in the battle with Santa Ana's overwhelmingly larger, stronger army, and the losses galvanized the remaining forces.  Davy Crockett was also killed in the battle.  
Texans are pretty protective of their history and traditions.  I explored getting a teaching certificate when we lived in Dallas.  (I had reciprocal credentials in Ohio and Georgia.)  I was told I could be certified once I had taken a class in Texas history...  srsly.

